$schema: https://usm.dev/schema/v1.json
$id: smith-gray/threshold-crypto
$type: feature
$version: 1
$last_updated: "2026-09-22"
summary: |
  Phase 2 hardening splits key knowledge between the secure element and the authority, reconstructs
  ephemerally only inside the element for a requested operation, and adds a hybrid classical plus
  ML-KEM-class ratchet on control-plane sessions with remote attestation before unwrap. No single
  compromised component holds enough to reconstruct a key.
$system: smith-gray/system
$service: smith-gray/sidecar
status: planned
intent: |
  A hardware root protects a key from a compromised host, but the device itself remains a single
  point of trust and long-lived ciphertext remains exposed to future quantum capability. Threshold
  splitting removes the single holder, and a post-quantum ratchet protects sessions against
  harvest-now-decrypt-later.

flows:
  - id: split-key-shares
    name: Split key knowledge across holders
    description: One share lives in the secure element; complementary shares live at the authority.
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: generate
        target: Provisioning splits key knowledge into shares with a threshold policy.
      - id: s2
        action: setup
        target: One share is installed in the secure element; complementary shares are held at the authority.
      - id: s3
        action: observe
        target: No single holder can reconstruct the key alone.
  - id: ephemeral-reconstruction
    name: Reconstruct ephemerally inside the element
    description: The key exists only inside the secure element for the duration of one operation.
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: receive
        target: Device receives an authorised operation request and attests remotely.
      - id: s2
        action: validate
        target: Remote attestation succeeds before any unwrap is permitted.
      - id: s3
        action: generate
        target: The key is reconstructed inside the element for the requested operation only.
      - id: s4
        action: delete
        target: The reconstructed material is destroyed when the operation completes.
  - id: hybrid-ratchet
    name: Hybrid post-quantum session ratchet
    description: Control-plane sessions use a classical plus PQ ratchet.
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: setup
        target: Negotiate a hybrid KEM combining a classical and an ML-KEM-class mechanism.
      - id: s2
        action: generate
        target: Ratchet session keys forward so compromise of one key does not expose past traffic.
      - id: s3
        action: observe
        target: Harvested session traffic is not decryptable by a future quantum adversary.

contracts:
  - id: no-single-holder
    description: No single component may be able to reconstruct the key.
    must_have:
      - Key knowledge is split with a threshold policy
      - The secure element alone is insufficient
      - The authority alone is insufficient
  - id: attest-before-unwrap
    description: Remote attestation is required before any unwrap.
    must_have:
      - Attestation covers device identity and state
      - Failure denies the operation
      - Attestation is not optional or bypassable
  - id: ephemeral-only
    description: Reconstructed key material exists only inside the secure element, only for one operation.
    must_have:
      - No reconstruction in host memory
      - Material is destroyed after the operation
      - Nothing persists between operations
  - id: post-quantum-sessions
    description: Control-plane sessions are protected against harvest-now-decrypt-later.
    must_have:
      - Hybrid classical plus PQ key establishment
      - Forward-secret ratcheting of session keys
      - Documented as Phase 2, not MVP

tests:
  - id: single-share-insufficient
    flow: split-key-shares
    setup:
      available_shares: 1
      threshold: 2
    expect:
      - assertion: reconstruction fails
      - assertion: no key material is produced
    contracts:
      - no-single-holder
  - id: unattested-device-denied
    flow: ephemeral-reconstruction
    setup:
      attestation: "fail"
    expect:
      - assertion: unwrap is denied
      - assertion: no reconstruction occurs
    contracts:
      - attest-before-unwrap
  - id: reconstruction-does-not-persist
    flow: ephemeral-reconstruction
    setup:
      operations: 2
    expect:
      - assertion: no reconstructed material survives between operations
      - assertion: host memory never contains the key
    contracts:
      - ephemeral-only
  - id: session-ratchet-forward-secret
    flow: hybrid-ratchet
    setup:
      compromise: "session key at time T"
    expect:
      - assertion: traffic before T is not decryptable
      - assertion: the hybrid KEM was used for establishment
    contracts:
      - post-quantum-sessions

decisions:
  - id: defer-to-phase-2
    decision: Keep threshold crypto and post-quantum ratchets out of the MVP and Phase 1.
    rationale: The MVP already meets the product promise with software isolation, and the blueprint is explicit that the agent-facing surface must not change when these land. Deferring keeps time to beta short without weakening the shipped guarantee.
    status: accepted
  - id: hybrid-not-pq-only
    decision: Use a hybrid classical plus ML-KEM-class construction rather than post-quantum only.
    rationale: Hybrid avoids depending entirely on relatively young PQ primitives while still closing the harvest-now-decrypt-later exposure.
    status: accepted
  - id: threshold-over-single-device
    decision: Split knowledge across element and authority rather than trusting a single device.
    rationale: A secure element is a strong boundary but still one holder; splitting means compromise of the device and compromise of the authority are both required, which is the difference between a breach and a non-event.
    status: accepted

implementation:
  primary: apps/sidecar/internal/verify
  test_code: ""
  test_code_status: none

see_also:
  - "smith-gray/hardware-root"
  - "smith-gray/envelope-encryption"
  - "smith-gray/sidecar-resolution"
